{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "nr-railroad-support-nation",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.5 step 7e, PENDING: the `nr-railroad-support-nation` RunSpec computed from the DEFAULT DATABASE -- the nation, August 2020, weekday, sector 12 (Railroad Support), onroad diesel, CO, NOx, SO2 and PM10. NONROAD's whole inventory at the nation: 1,119 equipment points, 5,777 cohorts, 23,108 rows, every key right and the shape recomputed.\n\n21,013 OF 23,108 CELLS REPRODUCE, and the rest is two residuals, both measured and neither explained. (1) Every GASOLINE SO2 cell -- 2,091 of them, 2- and 4-stroke, every model year -- is 1.38e-4 high, by one ratio (1.30 to 1.46e-4, which is the oracle's own rounding). The nation's gasoline sulfur is not it: the model's 0.00066419126 wt% and the `.OPT` func A query run against this run's execution database agree to 8e-7, and CO is exact, so the temperature and oxygen are not it either; the state and county runs' gasoline SO2 reproduces. (2) One diesel cohort, 2270002066 model year 2010, is 0.7 to 1.3e-4 off in all four pollutants by DIFFERENT amounts, which reads as a technology-mix effect in that one year.\n\nIt is here rather than in `runspecs/nonroad/` because `run-tests.sh` holds that directory to the oracle. The two folds `nr-commercial-nation` could not see -- the growth pattern's minimum over states and `nrUSMonthAllocation` -- this run's oracle does see, and it found the SEASON file's printed month fractions (PLAN.md §7.3.37) before these two were left."
  },
  "domain": {
    "element_type": "Float32"
  },
